-- הסכם קיבוצי מיום 23.3.2017 — עוז לתמורה, יישום עלות הסכם המסגרת לשנים
-- 2013–2016: the agreement between the Centre of Local Government and the
-- three large cities and ארגון המורים that sets out how the cost of the
-- application agreement of 20.3.2016 is spent on the teaching employees the
-- Oz LaTmura agreement covers — a monthly shekel supplement from 1.9.2016
-- (§4) and a new percentage supplement from 1.4.2017 (§5) — with the wages
-- commissioner's approval of it under §29(א) of the Budget Foundations Law
-- in front. Circular תשע"ז/4 carries both supplements out for the owners'
-- teachers in the high schools (l4/circulars/2016-17_tashaz_04.l4); the
-- application agreement of 20.3.2016 and the Oz LaTmura agreement's §56,
-- which this one exhausts, are named and not encoded here.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT minimum_wage_law

§ `הסכם קיבוצי מיום 23.3.2017 — יישום עלות הסכם ההחלה בעוז לתמורה`

§§ `אישור הממונה על השכר`

-- akn:preamble/p1 akn:preamble/p2 The Treasury's letterhead, the wages commissioner's; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p3 akn:preamble/p4 The letter's date, כ"ה באדר התשע"ז, 23 March 2017; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p5 The letter's file mark (שכ. 2017-15545); no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p6 akn:preamble/p7 akn:preamble/p8 akn:preamble/p9 akn:preamble/p10 akn:preamble/p11 akn:preamble/p12 The addressees: the Centre of Local Government's head of wage agreements and Jerusalem's head of human resources; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p13 The letter's subject, the approval of the agreement of 23.3.2017; no rule.

-- The wages commissioner approves the agreement under §29(א) of the Budget
-- Foundations Law, 1985: an agreement of the local authorities on wages
-- needs his approval, and this one has it, on the day it was signed.
@ref akn:preamble/p14
`the agreement of 23.3.2017 was approved under section 29 on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 23 3 2017
`the agreement of 23.3.2017 was signed on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 23 3 2017

#ASSERT `the agreement of 23.3.2017 was approved under section 29 on` EQUALS `the agreement of 23.3.2017 was signed on`

-- akn:preamble/p15 akn:preamble/p16 akn:preamble/p17 The sign-off and the signature of Eran Yaakov, the wages commissioner; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p18 akn:preamble/p19 akn:preamble/p20 akn:preamble/p21 akn:preamble/p22 The copies list; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p23 akn:preamble/p24 The Treasury's address and web pages; no rule.

§§ `המבוא`

-- akn:preamble/p25 akn:preamble/p26 The agreement's title and its day of signing, written in by hand (23/3/17); no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p27 akn:preamble/p28 akn:preamble/p29 akn:preamble/p30 The employers: the Centre of Local Government for every local authority save the three large cities, and the three large cities; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p31 akn:preamble/p32 akn:preamble/p33 The other side, ארגון המורים; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p34 A recital: the Oz LaTmura agreement of 14.8.2011 applies the cost of framework agreements signed with the Histadrut up to 31.12.2016 to its teachers, subject to an agreement between its parties.
-- akn:preamble/p35 A recital: the general framework agreement of 18.4.2016 for 1.1.2013–31.12.2017, amended on 8.8.2016 (l4/agreements/framework/2016-04-18_framework-agreement_public-sector.l4).
-- akn:preamble/p36 A recital: the application agreement of 20.3.2016 applies the relative cost to the Oz LaTmura teachers for 1.1.2013–31.12.2016 (outside the corpus).
-- akn:preamble/p37 A recital: that agreement set a cost frame and left its allocation to negotiation, with a default if none was agreed by the day set.
-- akn:preamble/p38 akn:preamble/p39 A recital that the parties agreed the allocation, and the words of agreement; no rule.

`what the agreement of 23.3.2017 rests on outside the corpus` MEANS
    LIST `outside the corpus` "הסכם ההחלה מיום 20.3.2016 (עלות הסכם המסגרת לעובדי ההוראה בעוז לתמורה)",
         `outside the corpus` "חוק שכר מינימום (העלאת סכומי שכר מינימום – הוראת שעה), התשע\"ה-2015"

§§ `1 כללי`

-- (א): the preamble is part of the agreement.
@ref akn:art_1__para_a
`the preamble of 23.3.2017 is part of the agreement` MEANS TRUE

-- (ב)–(ג): the masculine includes the feminine, the singular the plural,
-- and the other way round, unless said otherwise.
@ref akn:art_1__para_b akn:art_1__para_c
`the agreement of 23.3.2017 reads one gender and number for all` MEANS TRUE

-- (ד): the headings are for convenience and not read for meaning. (ה):
-- mentioning a letter does not change its normative standing.
@ref akn:art_1__para_d akn:art_1__para_e
`the agreement of 23.3.2017 reads its headings for meaning` MEANS FALSE
`mentioning a letter in the agreement of 23.3.2017 changes its standing` MEANS FALSE

§§ `2 תחולה`

-- §2: the teaching employees the application agreement covers.
@ref akn:art_2/p1
GIVEN `covered by the application agreement of 20.3.2016` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a teaching employee of 23.3.2017` `covered by the application agreement of 20.3.2016` IF
    `covered by the application agreement of 20.3.2016`

§§ `3 תקופת ההסכם`

-- §3: 1.1.2013 to 31.12.2016.
@ref akn:art_3/p1
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the period of 23.3.2017` d IF
    d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2013) AND d `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2016)

#ASSERT `in the period of 23.3.2017` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2016)
#ASSERT NOT `in the period of 23.3.2017` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2017)

§§ `4 תוספת שקלית לעובד הוראה`

-- (א)–(ב): from 1.9.2016, by §5(א)(1) of the application agreement, a
-- monthly shekel supplement; for a full position 108.74 to 31.3.2017,
-- 176.70 to 31.12.2017, 244.66 to 31.5.2018, 312.62 to 30.11.2018 and
-- 380.58 from 1.12.2018. F-oz-latmura-2017-03-23-a: (ד) updates "the
-- amount set above" every January from January 2017; the reading adopted
-- updates the amount in force on the update's day, each printed amount
-- paid as printed from its first day (convention dates.update-in-force).
@ref akn:art_4__para_a akn:art_4__para_b akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_1 akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_2 akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_3 akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_4 akn:art_4__para_b__subpara_5
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the full-position shekel supplement of 23.3.2017` d IS
    BRANCH IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2018) THEN 380.58
           IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2018) THEN 312.62
           IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2018) THEN 244.66
           IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2017) THEN 176.70
           IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016) THEN 108.74
           OTHERWISE 0

#ASSERT `the full-position shekel supplement of 23.3.2017` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016) EQUALS 108.74
#ASSERT `the full-position shekel supplement of 23.3.2017` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2017) EQUALS 108.74
#ASSERT `the full-position shekel supplement of 23.3.2017` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2018) EQUALS 380.58
#ASSERT 380.58 MINUS 312.62 EQUALS 312.62 MINUS 244.66

-- (ג): a part position, pro rata.
@ref akn:art_4__para_c
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the position share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the shekel supplement of 23.3.2017` d `the position share` IS
    `the full-position shekel supplement of 23.3.2017` d TIMES `the position share`

#ASSERT `the shekel supplement of 23.3.2017` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2017) 0.5 EQUALS 88.35

-- (ד): every January from January 2017, the amount set above rises by the
-- rise of the December index over the previous one (the first from
-- December 2015); a fall brings no update and is offset against the next
-- rise, measured from the last index used. The indices are the Central
-- Bureau of Statistics', inputs.
@ref akn:art_4__para_d akn:art_4__para_d/p2 akn:art_4__para_d/p3 akn:art_4__para_d/p4 akn:art_4__para_d/p5 akn:art_4__para_d/p6
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      `the new index` IS A NUMBER @desc December of the year before the update
      `the last index used` IS A NUMBER @desc the index of the last update made (December 2015 for the first)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the shekel supplement of 23.3.2017 as updated` amount `the new index` `the last index used` IS
    IF `the new index` GREATER THAN `the last index used`
    THEN amount TIMES `the new index` DIVIDED BY `the last index used`
    ELSE amount

#ASSERT `the shekel supplement of 23.3.2017 as updated` 100 102 100 EQUALS 102
#ASSERT `the shekel supplement of 23.3.2017 as updated` 100 99 100 EQUALS 100

-- F-oz-latmura-2017-03-23-a: the January 2017 update falls before 176.70
-- takes effect, and the January 2018 one on the day 244.66 does: read as
-- the base "set above", each printed amount is raised by the update of its
-- year; read as amounts set in advance, each is paid as printed. On a 2%
-- rise the two give 180.23 and 176.70.
`§4(ב)'s amounts and §4(ד)'s update give two readings` MEANS
        `the shekel supplement of 23.3.2017 as updated` 176.70 102 100 EQUALS 180.234
    AND NOT 180.234 EQUALS 176.70
#ASSERT `§4(ב)'s amounts and §4(ד)'s update give two readings`

DECLARE `what the 23.3.2017 shekel supplement might count for` IS ONE OF
    `topping up to the minimum wage, of 23.3.2017`
    `the hour value for substitution hours, of 23.3.2017`
    `the reduction for an hour of absence, of 23.3.2017`
    `severance pay, of 23.3.2017`
    `pension contributions under section 46 of the Oz LaTmura agreement, of 23.3.2017`
    `the study fund and the Dafna fund, of 23.3.2017`
    `the base of a wage supplement, percentage or shekel, of 23.3.2017`
    `the jubilee grant, of 23.3.2017`

-- not weighed against `the Severance Pay Law`: §§4(ו) and 5(ד) counts the
-- shekel supplement and the 2016 percentage supplement in the wage
-- severance is computed on. Which components count, §13 sends to the
-- regulations, which compute that wage by the collective agreement that
-- applies (as the takanon's §1.28.2.3 brings them); a component counted
-- adds to the severance and takes nothing the law gives (§31).

-- (ה): not counted toward the minimum-wage top-up, and an "excluded
-- supplement" of the temporary provision of 2015 (outside the corpus).
-- (ו): salary for every purpose — the hour value for substitution hours,
-- the reduction for an hour of absence, severance, pension contributions
-- under the Oz LaTmura agreement's §46, the study fund and Dafna. (ז): in
-- the base of no wage supplement; (ח): but counted for the jubilee grant.
@ref akn:art_4__para_e akn:art_4__para_f akn:art_4__para_g akn:art_4__para_h
GIVEN p IS A `what the 23.3.2017 shekel supplement might count for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 23.3.2017 shekel supplement counts for` p IF
        NOT p EQUALS `topping up to the minimum wage, of 23.3.2017`
    AND NOT p EQUALS `the base of a wage supplement, percentage or shekel, of 23.3.2017`

#ASSERT `the 23.3.2017 shekel supplement counts for` `the jubilee grant, of 23.3.2017`

-- (ט): paid from the salary for April 2017, paid in May 2017, "and no
-- later than the salary paid for May 2017 paid in April 2017", with the
-- differences from 1.9.2016. F-oz-latmura-2017-03-23-b: May's salary is
-- paid in June, and a salary paid in April cannot be later than April's
-- paid in May; the reading adopted is the salary for May paid in June, as
-- circular תשע"ז/4 prints it (convention reading.misprint). Time in salary
-- months from January 2017: April is 4, May 5.
@ref akn:art_4__para_i
`the first salary month of §4's payments` MEANS 4
`the last salary month of §4's payments` MEANS 5
`the month §4(ט)'s first salary is paid in` MEANS 5
`the month §4(ט)'s last salary is paid in, as printed` MEANS 4

`§4(ט)'s last salary is paid before its first` MEANS
    `the month §4(ט)'s last salary is paid in, as printed` LESS THAN `the month §4(ט)'s first salary is paid in`
#ASSERT `§4(ט)'s last salary is paid before its first`
#ASSERT `the last salary month of §4's payments` GREATER THAN `the first salary month of §4's payments`

§§ `5 תוספת אחוזית 2016`

-- (א): following §5(א)(2)–(5) of the application agreement, a new
-- percentage supplement: 0.625% from 1.4.2017, completed to 1.25% from
-- 1.1.2018, to 1.875% from 1.6.2018 and to 2.5% from 1.12.2018 ("תוספת
-- אחוזית 2016"). (ב): at one rate for every teaching employee.
@ref akn:art_5__para_a akn:art_5__para_a__subpara_1 akn:art_5__para_a__subpara_2 akn:art_5__para_a__subpara_3 akn:art_5__para_a__subpara_4 akn:art_5__para_a/p2 akn:art_5__para_b
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2016 percentage supplement rate of 23.3.2017` d IS
    BRANCH IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2018) THEN 2.5%
           IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2018) THEN 1.875%
           IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2018) THEN 1.25%
           IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2017) THEN 0.625%
           OTHERWISE 0

-- (ג): computed on the combined salary and the 2001, 2008, 2011, erosion
-- 2011 and Oz LaTmura supplements (the last where he is owed it).
@ref akn:art_5__para_c
GIVEN `the combined salary` IS A NUMBER
      `the 2001, 2008, 2011 and erosion 2011 supplements` IS A NUMBER
      `the Oz LaTmura supplement he is owed` IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2016 percentage supplement of 23.3.2017` `the combined salary` `the 2001, 2008, 2011 and erosion 2011 supplements` `the Oz LaTmura supplement he is owed` d IS
    `the 2016 percentage supplement rate of 23.3.2017` d
        TIMES (`the combined salary` PLUS `the 2001, 2008, 2011 and erosion 2011 supplements` PLUS `the Oz LaTmura supplement he is owed`)

#ASSERT `the 2016 percentage supplement of 23.3.2017` 8000 1500 500 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2018) EQUALS 250

DECLARE `what the 2016 percentage supplement of 23.3.2017 might count for` IS ONE OF
    `the percentage supplements on the combined salary but those of (ג) and the promotion-grade supplement, of 23.3.2017`
    `the 2001, 2008, 2011, erosion 2011, Oz LaTmura or promotion-grade supplement, of 23.3.2017`
    `the hour value for substitution hours, percentage supplement of 23.3.2017`
    `the reduction for an hour of absence, percentage supplement of 23.3.2017`
    `severance pay, percentage supplement of 23.3.2017`
    `pension contributions under section 46, percentage supplement of 23.3.2017`
    `the study fund and the Dafna fund, percentage supplement of 23.3.2017`
    `topping up to the minimum wage, percentage supplement of 23.3.2017`

-- (ד): counted for the percentage supplements on the combined salary save
-- the 2001, 2008, 2011, erosion 2011, Oz LaTmura and promotion-grade
-- supplements, and for the hour value for substitution hours, the
-- reduction for an hour of absence, severance, pension under §46, the
-- study fund and Dafna. (ו): not toward the minimum-wage top-up, and an
-- "excluded supplement" of the temporary provision of 2015.
@ref akn:art_5__para_d akn:art_5__para_f
GIVEN p IS A `what the 2016 percentage supplement of 23.3.2017 might count for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2016 percentage supplement of 23.3.2017 counts for` p IF
        NOT p EQUALS `the 2001, 2008, 2011, erosion 2011, Oz LaTmura or promotion-grade supplement, of 23.3.2017`
    AND NOT p EQUALS `topping up to the minimum wage, percentage supplement of 23.3.2017`

-- (ה): the 1987 and 1994 supplements are raised at (א)'s rates and days,
-- on their shekel value on the eve of the signing.
@ref akn:art_5__para_e
GIVEN `the supplement on the eve of 23.3.2017` IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 1987 or 1994 supplement after 23.3.2017` `the supplement on the eve of 23.3.2017` d IS
    `the supplement on the eve of 23.3.2017` TIMES (1 PLUS `the 2016 percentage supplement rate of 23.3.2017` d)

#ASSERT `the 1987 or 1994 supplement after 23.3.2017` 200 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2018) EQUALS 205

-- Against the Minimum Wage Law's floor (MMS-601): §4(ה) leaves the shekel
-- supplement out of the pay that counts toward the top-up and §5(ו) the
-- 2016 percentage supplement; leaving them out makes the top-up the law's
-- or more (its §11). Checked on a month's figures as if §3 counted each
-- (a fixed supplement for the work), the strictest case. That each is an
-- "excluded supplement" of the temporary provision of תשע"ה-2015 is
-- outside the pin (the provision has lapsed).
#ASSERT NOT `counting a component as the instrument does falls below the Minimum Wage Law` 5300 4800 (`component paid in the month under the Minimum Wage Law` `a fixed supplement paid for the work, under section 3(ב)(3)` 300) (`the 23.3.2017 shekel supplement counts for` `topping up to the minimum wage, of 23.3.2017`)
#ASSERT NOT `counting a component as the instrument does falls below the Minimum Wage Law` 5300 4800 (`component paid in the month under the Minimum Wage Law` `a fixed supplement paid for the work, under section 3(ב)(3)` 300) (`the 2016 percentage supplement of 23.3.2017 counts for` `topping up to the minimum wage, percentage supplement of 23.3.2017`)

§§ `6 מיצוי`

-- ¶1: §7 of the application agreement (its exhaustion of claims) applies
-- to this one too. ¶2: it reaches §5(א) and §5(ב) of the application
-- agreement as well, and no further negotiation is held on the Oz LaTmura
-- agreement's §56 or on the cost frame of the application agreement's §5(א).
@ref akn:art_6/p1 akn:art_6/p2
`negotiating further on §56 or the application agreement's frame, after 23.3.2017` MEANS FALSE

§§ `החתימות`

-- akn:conclusions/p1 akn:conclusions/p2 akn:conclusions/p3 akn:conclusions/p4 The signatures of ארגון המורים, the Centre of Local Government and the three large cities; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p5 A file number printed at the foot (2016-27787); no rule.
